IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lss-core`
IMPORT `lss-seat-owner-driver`

-- Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) -- cases for the owner's or driver's seat
-- (lss-seat-owner-driver.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from ss 45 and 46 of the deposited text, never
-- copied from the encoding's output. Figures: the Authority has paid $200 000 and estimates future payments with a
-- present value of $800 000, so the present value of its liabilities is $1 000 000 (s 45(4)).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the owner or driver`

§§ `s 45: can the Authority recover from me`

`owner` MEANS `the owner of the vehicle, and someone else was driving`
`driver` MEANS `the driver of the vehicle, and not its owner`
`owner-driver` MEANS `the owner and the driver of the vehicle`
`third` MEANS `another person partly at fault, not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle`

`r full` MEANS `yes: the Authority may recover from you as a debt the present value of its treatment, care and support liabilities for the injury, reduced for the participant's contributory negligence; where the owner and someone else as driver are both liable, jointly or either of you severally (s 45(1), (2), (4), (5))`
`r share` MEANS `yes: the Authority may recover from you as a debt the share of the present value of its treatment, care and support liabilities that corresponds to your share in the responsibility for the injury (s 45(3), (4))`
`r not participant` MEANS `no: the Authority recovers under s 45 only the costs of the injury of a participant in the Scheme (s 45(1))`
`r s6` MEANS `no: the Authority may not recover where the participant paid an amount to the Authority under s 6 for those injuries (s 45(10))`
`r not at fault` MEANS `not covered: s 45(3) reaches a person, other than an owner or driver, who was partly at fault for the injury`
`r no fault` MEANS `no: s 45(1) applies only if the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver of a motor vehicle in its use or operation (s 45(1)(a))`
`r insured` MEANS `no: s 45(1) applies only if the vehicle was not insured as Part 4 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 requires at the time of the accident (s 45(1)(b))`
`r exempt` MEANS `no: the Authority may not recover from the owner or driver of a vehicle that was not required to be registered, was exempt from registration, or was not required to be insured (s 45(8))`
`r owner defence` MEANS `no: you have a sufficient defence as owner if you establish to the court's satisfaction that someone else was driving without your authority (s 45(6))`
`r driver defence` MEANS `no: you have a sufficient defence as driver if you establish to the court's satisfaction that you drove with the owner's authority (or reasonably believed you had it) and reasonably believed the vehicle was insured as Part 4 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 requires (s 45(7))`

-- Argument order: role, participant, bought in under s 6, fault of owner or driver, uninsured, not required to be
-- registered or insured, I was partly at fault, owner's defence, driver's defence.
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `owner` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r full`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `driver` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r full`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `owner-driver` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r full`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `owner` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r not participant`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `owner` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r s6`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `driver` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r no fault`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `driver` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r insured`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `owner-driver` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r exempt`
-- s 45(6): the owner's defence; it does not help a driver, and an owner who drove has none (fork F12).
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `owner` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `r owner defence`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `driver` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `r full`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `owner-driver` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `r full`
-- s 45(7): the driver's defence; it does not help an owner.
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `driver` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `r driver defence`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `owner` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `r full`
-- s 45(3): another person partly at fault (fork F7: not limited to an uninsured vehicle).
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `third` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r share`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `third` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r not at fault`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` `third` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r s6`

§§ `s 45: how much`

-- Full recovery, no contributory negligence: $1 000 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most the Authority can recover from me` `owner` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 800000 0 0 EQUALS 1000000
-- s 45(2): the participant 25% responsible: $750 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most the Authority can recover from me` `driver` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 800000 25 0 EQUALS 750000
-- The participant wholly responsible: nothing.
#ASSERT `What is the most the Authority can recover from me` `driver` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 800000 100 0 EQUALS 0
-- s 45(3): a third person 40% responsible: $400 000 (the participant's own share does not reduce it further).
#ASSERT `What is the most the Authority can recover from me` `third` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 200000 800000 25 40 EQUALS 400000
-- A defence, an insured vehicle, a s 6 buy-in: nothing.
#ASSERT `What is the most the Authority can recover from me` `owner` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 200000 800000 0 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the most the Authority can recover from me` `owner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 800000 0 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the most the Authority can recover from me` `owner` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 800000 0 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 46: persons in default`

#ASSERT `Can the Authority use my insurer's right of recovery against me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Authority may exercise against you the same right of recovery the insurer or nominal defendant has under s 116 or s 124A of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959, for the present value of its treatment, care and support liabilities for the participant (s 46(1), (2), (4))`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority use my insurer's right of recovery against me` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 46 applies only if an approved insurer or the nominal defendant has a right of recovery against you under s 116 or s 124A of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (s 46(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority use my insurer's right of recovery against me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 46 applies only if the injured person becomes a participant in the Scheme (s 46(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can the Authority use my insurer's right of recovery against me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 46 applies only if an approved insurer or the nominal defendant has a right of recovery against you under s 116 or s 124A of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (s 46(1)(a))`
